Windows (cosmo): open mkfs.fat's target without O_EXCL.

mkfs.fat opens its target with `O_EXCL | O_RDWR` to refuse a mounted or busy
block device. On a regular file without O_CREAT, O_EXCL is a no-op on Linux,
but cosmocc's NT open() rejects it with EINVAL ("unable to open ...: Invalid
argument"). On Windows the target is always an image file, so O_EXCL becomes
0 there (e2fsprogs' unix_io.c needs the same). wine tolerates O_EXCL, so only
a real Windows host shows the failure.

--- a/src/mkfs.fat.c
+++ b/src/mkfs.fat.c
@@ -49,6 +49,10 @@
 #include "version.h"
 
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+#undef O_EXCL
+#define O_EXCL 0
+#endif
 #include <signal.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
